@startuml GupShup Cafe - Database ER Diagram

!define TABLE(name) entity name << (T,#FFAAAA) >>
!define PRIMARY_KEY(x) <u>x</u>
!define FOREIGN_KEY(x) <i>x</i>

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam classBackgroundColor LightYellow
skinparam classBorderColor DarkBlue

title GupShup Cafe - Database Schema (MVP - SQLite on EFS)

' Users table
entity "users" as users {
  PRIMARY_KEY(id) : TEXT (UUID)
  --
  email : TEXT (UNIQUE)
  current_cefr_level : TEXT
  topic_interests : TEXT (JSON array)
  created_at : DATETIME
  last_active : DATETIME
  --
  **NOT IN MVP:**
  total_sessions : INTEGER
  total_speaking_time : INTEGER
  avg_grammar_score : REAL
  avg_vocabulary_score : REAL
  avg_fluency_score : REAL
}

' Sessions table
entity "sessions" as sessions {
  PRIMARY_KEY(id) : TEXT (UUID)
  --
  room_code : TEXT (UNIQUE)
  topic : TEXT
  topic_category : TEXT
  max_participants : INTEGER
  speaking_time_per_turn : INTEGER
  num_rounds : INTEGER
  status : TEXT
  current_round : INTEGER
  current_speaker_index : INTEGER
  FOREIGN_KEY(created_by) : TEXT
  started_at : DATETIME
  ended_at : DATETIME
  duration_seconds : INTEGER
  created_at : DATETIME
}

' Participants table
entity "participants" as participants {
  PRIMARY_KEY(id) : TEXT (UUID)
  --
  FOREIGN_KEY(session_id) : TEXT
  FOREIGN_KEY(user_id) : TEXT
  anonymous_name : TEXT
  avatar_color : TEXT
  role : TEXT
  is_ready : BOOLEAN
  socket_id : TEXT
  starting_cefr_level : TEXT
  ending_cefr_level : TEXT
  joined_at : DATETIME
  left_at : DATETIME
  --
  **NOT IN MVP:**
  total_speaking_time : INTEGER
  total_words_spoken : INTEGER
  number_of_turns : INTEGER
}

' Transcripts table
entity "transcripts" as transcripts {
  PRIMARY_KEY(id) : TEXT (UUID)
  --
  FOREIGN_KEY(session_id) : TEXT
  FOREIGN_KEY(participant_id) : TEXT
  FOREIGN_KEY(user_id) : TEXT
  text : TEXT
  turn_number : INTEGER
  round_number : INTEGER
  timestamp : DATETIME
  duration_seconds : INTEGER
  word_count : INTEGER
}

' Feedback table
entity "feedback" as feedback {
  PRIMARY_KEY(id) : TEXT (UUID)
  --
  FOREIGN_KEY(session_id) : TEXT
  FOREIGN_KEY(participant_id) : TEXT
  FOREIGN_KEY(user_id) : TEXT
  FOREIGN_KEY(transcript_id) : TEXT
  feedback_type : TEXT
  grammar_issues : TEXT (JSON)
  vocabulary_suggestions : TEXT (JSON)
  fluency_comments : TEXT
  suggestions : TEXT (JSON)
  strengths : TEXT (JSON)
  display_message : TEXT
  agent_mention : TEXT
  agent_model : TEXT
  generation_time_ms : INTEGER
  created_at : DATETIME
  --
  **NOT IN MVP:**
  cefr_level : TEXT
  grammar_score : REAL
  vocabulary_score : REAL
  fluency_score : REAL
  overall_score : REAL
}

' Topics table (for AI generation tracking)
entity "topics" as topics {
  PRIMARY_KEY(id) : TEXT (UUID)
  --
  topic_text : TEXT
  category : TEXT
  generated_by : TEXT
  used_count : INTEGER
  created_at : DATETIME
  last_used_at : DATETIME
}

' Analytics table (optional, for aggregated stats)
entity "analytics" as analytics {
  PRIMARY_KEY(id) : TEXT (UUID)
  --
  metric_name : TEXT
  metric_value : REAL
  dimensions : TEXT (JSON)
  timestamp : DATETIME
  aggregation_period : TEXT
}

' Relationships
users ||--o{ participants : "participates in"
sessions ||--o{ participants : "contains"
users ||--o{ sessions : "creates"
sessions ||--o{ transcripts : "has"
participants ||--o{ transcripts : "speaks"
participants ||--o{ feedback : "receives"
sessions ||--o{ feedback : "generates"
transcripts ||--o| feedback : "analyzed in"
sessions }o--|| topics : "uses"

note right of users
  **User Model:**
  - Stores long-term progress
  - CEFR level tracking
  - Topic preferences
  - OAuth identity (email)
  
  **MVP Simplification:**
  - No complex statistics
  - No avatar/profile pics
  - Basic CEFR tracking only
end note

note right of sessions
  **Session Model:**
  - Represents a discussion room
  - Tracks real-time state
  - Links to participants
  
  **Status values:**
  - "waiting" : Lobby phase
  - "in_progress" : Discussion active
  - "completed" : Finished normally
  - "cancelled" : Ended early
  
  **Configuration:**
  - Default: 3 participants
  - Default: 60s speaking time
  - Default: 3 rounds
end note

note right of participants
  **Participant Model:**
  - Per-session identity
  - Anonymous names (privacy)
  - Role-based permissions
  
  **Roles:**
  - "host" : Created room
  - "participant" : Regular speaker
  - "listener" : Future feature
  
  **Real-time fields:**
  - socket_id : Socket.io connection
  - is_ready : Ready to start
end note

note right of transcripts
  **Transcript Model:**
  - Raw speech-to-text output
  - Timestamped per turn
  - Links to participant & session
  
  **Usage:**
  - Real-time display
  - LLM analysis input
  - Post-session review
  - Export functionality
  
  **Storage:**
  - TEXT field (no length limit)
  - Indexed by session_id
  - Ordered by timestamp
end note

note right of feedback
  **Feedback Model:**
  - AI-generated analysis
  - Two types: instant & comprehensive
  
  **Instant Feedback:**
  - 2-3 second response
  - Per transcript
  - Real-time modal display
  
  **Comprehensive Feedback:**
  - Post-discussion analysis
  - All transcripts analyzed
  - Progress tracking
  - Recommendations
  
  **JSON fields:**
  - grammar_issues: Array of corrections
  - vocabulary_suggestions: Alternatives
  - suggestions: Actionable tips
  - strengths: Positive highlights
end note

note as DatabaseImplementation
  **Database Implementation (MVP):**
  
  **Technology:**
  - SQLite (lightweight, serverless)
  - Stored on AWS EFS (shared across Fargate tasks)
  - Path: /mnt/efs/data/roundtable.db
  
  **Async Access:**
  - aiosqlite library for async operations
  - Connection pooling for concurrency
  - Transactions for consistency
  
  **Indexes:**
  - sessions.room_code (UNIQUE)
  - participants.session_id
  - transcripts.session_id
  - feedback.session_id
  - feedback.participant_id
  
  **Constraints:**
  - Foreign keys enforced
  - NOT NULL on required fields
  - UNIQUE on email, room_code
  - CHECK on CEFR levels (A0-C2)
  
  **Migrations:**
  - Manual SQL scripts for schema changes
  - Version tracking in migrations table
  
  **Backup Strategy:**
  - EFS automatic backups
  - Daily SQLite .backup command
  - Archived sessions after 30 days
  
  **Performance:**
  - 1000s of concurrent sessions
  - Sub-millisecond queries
  - Adequate for MVP scale
  
  **Future Considerations:**
  - Migrate to PostgreSQL for production scale
  - Add full-text search (FTS5)
  - Partitioning by date
  - Separate read replicas
end note

note as QueryExamples
  **Common Queries:**
  
  **Get User's Recent Sessions:**
  ```sql
  SELECT s.* FROM sessions s
  JOIN participants p ON s.id = p.session_id
  WHERE p.user_id = ? AND s.status = 'completed'
  ORDER BY s.ended_at DESC LIMIT 10;
  ```
  
  **Get Session with Participants:**
  ```sql
  SELECT s.*, p.anonymous_name, p.role
  FROM sessions s
  JOIN participants p ON s.id = p.session_id
  WHERE s.room_code = ?;
  ```
  
  **Get Transcripts for Session:**
  ```sql
  SELECT t.*, p.anonymous_name
  FROM transcripts t
  JOIN participants p ON t.participant_id = p.id
  WHERE t.session_id = ?
  ORDER BY t.timestamp ASC;
  ```
  
  **Get User's CEFR Progress:**
  ```sql
  SELECT 
    p.starting_cefr_level,
    p.ending_cefr_level,
    s.ended_at
  FROM participants p
  JOIN sessions s ON p.session_id = s.id
  WHERE p.user_id = ?
  ORDER BY s.ended_at ASC;
  ```
  
  **Analytics - Topic Usage:**
  ```sql
  SELECT topic_category, COUNT(*) as count
  FROM sessions
  WHERE status = 'completed'
  GROUP BY topic_category
  ORDER BY count DESC;
  ```
end note

@enduml
